d Labs brand associated with the product announcement, not a generated scene or a third-party company logo. The SVG is the official site icon linked in https://www.worldlabs.ai/ HTML.","Source reviewed","2026-10-19","verified","Year","2025","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[109,286],"dimensions","Development stages",[1334,1335,286],"stages","Assets & animation","Engines & scenes","Topics",[1339,1340,1341,1342,1343],"tags","scene-generation","explicit-3d","Gaussian-splatting","mesh-export","hosted","Further reading",[1346,1347],{"_73":1350,"_50":1351},{"_73":1348,"_50":1349},"Web-app mesh export","https://docs.worldlabs.ai/marble/export/mesh","Product","https://marble.worldlabs.ai/","Project source",[1354],{"_73":1352,"_50":967},"Why it belongs here","Marble supports multimodal world creation, exports Gaussian splats, visual meshes, and collision meshes for approximate physics, and renders video along camera paths. Compared with pure video continuation, it produces spatial assets for downstream engines. Developers still need to build character behavior, quest logic, and game loops. According to the inspected web-app guide, collider mesh export is included with Standard and high-quality textured GLB export requires Pro.","detail","Resource type","Tool","Category","category","summary","name","tool",[1371,1372],[1339,1340,1341,1342,1343],[166,1370,293],[126,293],2025,"scene",{"_73":1350,"_50":1351},{"_73":1348,"_50":1349},"resource:wonderworld","Builds an explorable, expandable explicit 3D scene from a single image.",{"_44":821,"_1363":818,"_1361":293,"_71":1412,"_1362":1374,"_1357":1410,"_50":1409,"_81":1413,"_1338":1414,"_1333":1415,"_1330":1416,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1395},[1377,1378,1379,1380,1381,1382,1383,1384,1385,1386,1387,1388,1389,1390],{"_71":46,"_75":818,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":1374,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":286,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1411,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":1410,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":1407,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":1403,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":1399,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":1398,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":1397,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1396,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":1394},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":1391},[1392],{"_73":1393,"_50":809},"Stanford University","The author page lists equal-contribution first authors Hong-Xing (Koven) Yu and Haoyi Duan at Stanford University, with MIT also represented. Select Stanford. The logo is the official touch icon linked by https://identity.stanford.edu/.","2026-10-18","2024",[109,286],[1334,1335,286],[1339,1340,1400,1401,1402],"Gaussian-surfels","camera-control","CVPR-2025",[1404],{"_73":1405,"_50":1406},"Project","https://kovenyu.com/WonderWorld/",[1408],{"_73":1352,"_50":1409},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09394","Interactive 3D Scene Generation from a Single Image uses Fast Layered Gaussian Surfels and guided depth diffusion to connect new scenes as the camera moves and prompts change. It provides explicit spatial representation and real-time rendering, primarily addressing geometry and appearance. Interactive gameplay, physics, and persistent dynamic state still require separate implementation.","Paper","paper",[1418],[1339,1340,1400,1401,1402],[166,1370,293],[126,293],2024,{"_73":1405,"_50":1406},"resource:oasis","oasis","Oasis: A Universe in a Transformer","A neural game research release that predicts Minecraft-style frames from prior frames and actions.","/resources/oasis/",{"_44":1420,"_1363":1421,"_1361":293,"_71":1465,"_1362":1422,"_1357":1463,"_50":1443,"_81":1466,"_1338":1467,"_1333":1468,"_1330":1469,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1320},[1426,1427,1428,1429,1430,1431,1432,1433,1434,1435,1436,1437,1438,1439],{"_71":46,"_