tion examples do not include the full hosted service or a complete game project.",[3629,3630,3631],{"_2286":3626,"_43":3627,"_57":3628},[3603,3604,3605,3606,3161],[166,1370],[247,126],{"_73":3597,"_50":3598,"_42":2286,"_2282":3599},{"_73":3592,"_50":3593,"_42":3072,"_2282":3594},{"_73":3588,"_50":3584,"_42":3066,"_2282":3589},{"_73":3615,"_50":3616},{"_73":3613,"_50":3614},{"_73":3611,"_50":3612},"resource:tripo-generation-api","tripo-generation-api","Tripo Model Generation API","Versioned text-to-model generation with separate geometry and texture seeds.","/resources/tripo-generation-api/",{"_44":3633,"_1363":3634,"_1361":126,"_71":1364,"_1362":3635,"_1357":3666,"_50":3655,"_81":3668,"_1338":3669,"_1333":3670,"_1330":3671,"_1321":1320},[3639,3640,3641,3642,3643,3644,3645,3646,3647,3648,3649,3650,3651],{"_71":46,"_75":3634,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3635,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3666,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3664,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3660,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3658,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3657,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3656,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1320,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":2361},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3652},[3653],{"_73":3654,"_50":3655},"Tripo AI / VAST","https://docs.tripo3d.ai/model-generation/text-to-model-v3-0-v3-1.html",[109],[1334],[3659],"asset-generation",[3661],{"_73":3662,"_50":3663},"Tripo task results","https://docs.tripo3d.ai/task-query/get-your-task-result.html",[3665],{"_73":1352,"_50":3655},"H3 text-to-model requests (v3.1-20260211 and v3.0-20250812) expose separate geometry and texture seeds plus PBR controls. Persist model_version and task ID, query with the submitting API key, and download successful output files promptly: their URLs expire after five minutes by default. Low-poly generation can fail on complex inputs. Cross-version reproducibility, output rights, cancellation endpoints and retry charges remain unverified.","3D development",[3672],[3659],[166],[126],{"_73":3662,"_50":3663},"resource:unigen","unigen","UniGen","Plans Unity prototypes, generates scripts, assembles scenes, and supports iterative debugging.","/resources/unigen/",{"_44":3674,"_1363":3675,"_1361":126,"_71":1465,"_1362":3676,"_1357":3730,"_50":3703,"_81":3731,"_2277":3732,"_1338":3733,"_1333":3734,"_1330":3735,"_1324":1369,"_1321":1395},[3680,3681,3682,3683,3684,3685,3686,3687,3688,3689,3690,3691,3692,3693,3694,3695,3696,3697,3698,3699],{"_71":46,"_75":3675,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3676,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3730,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3728,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3725,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3721,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3720,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3719,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1323,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":81,"_73":2286,"_83":3714,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":2275,"_75":2286,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":43,"_83":3709,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":2275,"_75":93,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":57,"_83":3705,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":2275,"_75":3286,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":3704},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3700},[3701],{"_73":3702,"_50":3703},"yxwan123","https://github.com/yxwan123/UniGen","The public implementation is maintained by yxwan123. No independent project mark or institutional affiliation was verified from the repository. Show the real maintainer name; do not substitute an account portrait, identicon, or engine logo.",[3706],{"_73":3707,"_50":3703,"_2282":3708},"Pipeline source","Published generator implementation and prompts; this is not a complete release of every benchmark game.",[3710],{"_73":3711,"_50":3712,"_2282":3713},"Unity generation video","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xyJjFfnxUx0","Author-linked demonstration video, not a browser-playable game.",[3715],{"_73":3716,"_50":3717,"_2282":3718},"Installation and usage","https://github.com/yxwan123/UniGen#-installation","README covers prerequisites and the local Unity generation workflow; review paths and project setup before running.",[109],[1637,1447,1335,1545],[3229,3722,3723,3724],"Game generation","Scene assembly","Research prototype",[3726],{"_73":1411,"_50":3727},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.26161",[3729],{"_73":1352,"_50":3703},"A multi-agent research workflow for Unity game creation from natural-language descriptions. The repository publishes its Python pipeline and model connector, with installation guidance and a recorded demonstration. Unity and a model-service account are required. Public pipeline code is available, but a hosted playable build and complete downloadable versions of the benchmark games were not verified.",[3739],{"_2286":3736,"_43":3737,"_57":3738},[3229,3722,3723,3724],[1653,1470,1370,1562],[126],{"_73":3716,"_50":3717,"_42":2286,"_2282":3718},{"_73":3711,"_50":3712,"_42":93,"_2282":3713},{"_73":3707,"_50":3703,"_42":3332,"_2282":3708},{"_73":1411,"_50":3727},"resource:autoue","Coordinates agents to build Unreal scenes, gameplay code, interactions, and playtests.",{"_44":716,"_1363":712,"_1361":126,"_71":1465,"_1362":3741,"_1357":3796,"_50":703,"_81":3797,"_2277":3798,"_1338":3799,"_1333":3800,"_1330":3801,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1320},[3744,3745,3746,3747,3748,3749,3750,3751,3752,3753,3754,3755,3756,3757,3758,3759,3760,3761,3762,3763],{"_71":46,"_75":712,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3741,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3796,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3794,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3785,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3783,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3782,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3781,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1320,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":81,"_73":2286,"_83":3776,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":2275,"_75":2286,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":43,"_83":3771,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":2275,"_75":93,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":57,"_83":3768,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":2275,"_75":3286,"_77":2277,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":3767},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3764},[3765],{"_73":3766,"_50":703},"Pluto156","The public implementation is maintained by Pluto156. No independent project mark or institutional affiliation was verified from the repository. Show the real maintainer name; do not substitute an account portrait, identicon, or engine logo.",[3769],{"_73":3707,"_50":703,"_2282":3770},"Public framework implementation; engine setup, model services, and dataset assets remain separate requirements.",[3772],{"_73":3773,"_50":3774,"_2282":3775},"Game-generation video","https://github.com/Pluto156/AutoUE/blob/main/assets/show.mp4","Recorded demonstrations of generated Unreal games; no public browser-playable build verified.",[3777],{"_73":3778,"_50":3779,"_2282":3780},"Setup and usage","https://github.com/Pluto156/AutoUE#setup-and-usage","Author instructions for dependencies, service credentials, and running the Unreal generation pipeline.",[109],[1637,1447,1334,1335,1545],[715,3722,3784,3724],"Multi-agent",[3786,3787,3788],{"_73":1411,"_50":3793},{"_73":3791,"_50":3792},{"_73":3789,"_50":3790},"Pinned evaluation dispatcher","https://github.com/Pluto156/AutoUE/blob/8686a4d51c19813f2b3368bd73f685a940db7531/PCGGen_UE/Plugins/LLMEditor/Source/LLMEditor/Private/Core/EvaluateExecutor/EvaluateExecutor.cpp#L174-L186","Generated games and asset dataset","https://huggingface.co/datasets/Pluto156/AutoUE_DataSet","https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.07106",[3795],{"_73":1352,"_50":703},"A research pipeline for turning a game description into Unreal Engine scenes and C++ gameplay. Its public implementation includes setup instructions, a demonstration video, and a linked dataset of generated games and assets. Reproduction requires Unreal integrations and external model services. The video demonstrates outputs; it is not a hosted playable game. Static inspection of the pinned evaluation dispatcher shows movement commands skipped and interaction handlers called directly; completion of that script path alone does not establish player navigation success.",[3805,3806,3807],{"_2286":3802,"_43":3803,"_57":3804},[715,3722,3784,3724],[1653,1470,166,1370,1562],[126],{"_73":3778,"_50":3779,"_42":2286,"_2282":3780},{"_73":3773,"_50":3774,"_42":93,"_2282":3775},{"_73":3707,"_50":703,"_42":3332,"_2282":3770},{"_73":1411,"_50":3793},{"_73":3791,"_50":3792},{"_73":3789,"_50":3790},"resource:blenderllm","blenderllm","BlenderLLM / BlendNet / CADBench","Studies text-to-Blender scripting with a training dataset and modeling benchmark.","/resources/blenderllm/",{"_44":3809,"_1363":3810,"_1361":126,"_71":1412,"_1362":3811,"_1357":3854,"_50":3832,"_81":3855,"_1338":3856,"_1333":3857,"_1330":3858,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1320},[3815,3816,3817,3818,3819,3820,3821,3822,3823,3824,3825,3826,3827,3828],{"_71":46,"_75":3810,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3811,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1411,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3854,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3852,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3841,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3836,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3835,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3834,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1396,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1320,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":3833},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3829},[3830],{"_73":3831,"_50":3832},"The Chinese University of Hong Kong, Shenzhen · School of Data Science","https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/BlenderLLM","The official README's About section explicitly says the team is from the School of Data Science, CUHK Shenzhen. The university logo is linked on its official English homepage. CUHK Shenzhen is identified distinctly from CUHK in Hong Kong.",[109],[1334,1545],[3837,3838,3839,3840],"Text-to-bpy","CADBench","Dataset","Modeling benchmark",[3842,3843,3844,3845],{"_73":1411,"_50":3851},{"_73":3849,"_50":3850},{"_73":3838,"_50":3848},{"_73":3846,"_50":3847},"Pinned release dataset description","https://github.com/FreedomIntelligence/BlenderLLM/blob/f778bfd6992ddd675f7615d0eaf965a8576f2879/README.md#L44-L50","https://huggingface.co/datasets/FreedomIntelligence/CADBench","BlendNet dataset","https://huggingface.co/datasets/FreedomIntelligence/BlendNet","https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.14203",[3853],{"_73":1352,"_50":3832},"BlenderLLM generates bpy modeling scripts from user instructions. The repository and released dataset documentation report about 12K BlendNet pairs, and CADBench includes synthetic and forum-sourced tasks. Evaluation focuses on basic CAD-style modeling and instruction following. The README identifies limitations in advanced materials, multimodal input, and multi-turn collaboration; this is not a game creation benchmark.",[3859,3860,3861,3862],[3837,3838,3839,3840],[166,1562],[126],{"_73":1411,"_50":3851},{"_73":3849,"_50":3850},{"_73":3838,"_50":3848},{"_73":3846,"_50":3847},"resource:video2game","Reconstructs real-world video into interactive 3D environments for the browser.",{"_44":858,"_1363":854,"_1361":126,"_71":1412,"_1362":3864,"_1357":3901,"_50":3900,"_81":3902,"_1338":3903,"_1333":3904,"_1330":3905,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1320},[3867,3868,3869,3870,3871,3872,3873,3874,3875,3876,3877,3878,3879,3880],{"_71":46,"_75":854,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3864,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1411,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3901,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3898,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3892,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3888,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3887,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3886,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1396,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1320,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":3885},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3881},[3882],{"_73":3883,"_50":3884},"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign","https://arxiv.org/html/2404.09833","The paper lists first author Hongchi Xia at both UIUC and Shanghai Jiao Tong University, with coauthors at UIUC and Cornell. UIUC is one verified first-author affiliation. This is its official brand CDN icon, linked by illinois.edu.",[109],[1334,1335,286],[3889,3890,893,3891],"Video-to-3D","Reconstruction","Collision",[3893,3894],{"_73":1411,"_50":3897},{"_73":3895,"_50":3896},"Pinned engine-handoff recommendations","https://github.com/video2game/video2game/blob/7bcf8ae754240b9fd2de75a154eb73c75a146b79/readme.md#L256-L273","https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.09833",[3899],{"_73":1352,"_50":3900},"https://github.com/video2game/video2game","Video and camera information pass through reconstruction, mesh extraction, appearance baking, and collision generation into a three.js game environment. The documented UE route recommends fully diffuse baked meshes, with the baking specular dimension set to zero. This is an explicit environment reconstruction approach with remaining manual scene setup and physics integration. It should be distinguished from interactive video world models that predict the next frame.",[3906,3907],[3889,3890,893,3891],[166,1370,293],[126],{"_73":1411,"_50":3897},{"_73":3895,"_50":3896},"resource:holodeck","Lays out and furnishes interactive 3D indoor environments from text.",{"_44":129,"_1363":116,"_1361":126,"_71":1465,"_1362":3909,"_1357":3946,"_50":3945,"_81":3947,"_1338":3948,"_1333":3949,"_1330":3950,"_1324":3951,"_1321":1395},[3912,3913,3914,3915,3916,3917,3918,3919,3920,3921,3922,3923,3924,3925,3926],{"_71":46,"_75":116,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3909,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3946,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3943,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3940,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3935,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3934,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3933,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":3932,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":1591,"_77":1592,"_73":1593,"_94":97,"_103":102,"_57":87,"_78":76},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":3931},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3927},[3928],{"_73":3929,"_50":3930},"Allen Institute for AI · Ai2","https://arxiv.org/html/2312.09067","The official code is hosted by allenai, and the paper lists multiple Allen Institute authors alongside collaborators at UPenn, Stanford, and the University of Washington. The icon comes from Ai2's official homepage. This represents the code-hosting research institution, not an exclusive affiliation for every author.","2023",[109],[1637,1335],[3936,3937,3938,3939],"Text-to-scene","AI2-THOR","Spatial constraints","Embodied environments",[3941],{"_73":1411,"_50":3942},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.09067",[3944],{"_73":1352,"_50":3945},"https://github.com/allenai/Holodeck","Combines language planning, asset retrieval, and spatial constraints to turn room requirements into AI2-THOR scenes, with instructions for loading them in Unity. Evaluation primarily targets embodied AI environment generation. It offers ideas for scene layout and semantic interaction, but does not establish complete game level design or commercial release readiness.",[3952],[3936,3937,3938,3939],[1653,1370],[126],2023,{"_73":1411,"_50":3942},"resource:infinigen","Procedurally generates natural and indoor Blender scenes and synthetic data.",{"_44":167,"_1363":161,"_1361":126,"_71":1465,"_1362":3954,"_1357":3989,"_50":3975,"_81":3990,"_1338":3991,"_1333":3992,"_1330":3993,"_1324":3951,"_1321":1395},[3957,3958,3959,3960,3961,3962,3963,3964,3965,3966,3967,3968,3969,3970,3971],{"_71":46,"_75":161,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3954,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":3989,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":3987,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":3984,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":3980,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":3979,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":3978,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":3932,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":1591,"_77":1592,"_73":1593,"_94":156,"_103":3977,"_57":152,"_78":149},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":3976},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":3972},[3973],{"_73":3974,"_50":3975},"Princeton University · Vision & Learning Lab","https://github.com/princeton-vl/infinigen","The official repository is maintained by Princeton Vision & Learning Lab. The lab's official cs.princeton.edu homepage links this orange lab icon. It is the real lab identity rather than a reconstructed university seal.","Official Infinigen samples of procedurally generated forests, underwater scenes, deserts, and mountains",[109],[1334,1335,1545],[2453,3981,3982,3983],"Blender","Synthetic data","Scenes",[3985],{"_73":3986,"_50":152},"Project and paper",[3988],{"_73":1352,"_50":3975},"Random seeds, parameters, and asset generators produce geometry, materials, scenes, and annotations, with export documentation for OBJ, OpenUSD, and other formats. This is a procedural system rather than a language model. It can provide controllable scenes and data for AI development workflows; real-time games still need optimization, collision, and gameplay integration.",[3994],[2453,3981,3982,3983],[166,1370,1562],[126],{"_73":3986,"_50":152},"resource:triposr","Quickly reconstructs a 3D object from one image for asset prototyping.",{"_44":607,"_1363":604,"_1361":126,"_71":1364,"_1362":3996,"_1357":4023,"_50":594,"_1338":4024,"_1333":4025,"_1330":4026,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1395},[3999,4000,4001,4002,4003,4004,4005,4006,4007,4008,4009,4010,4011],{"_71":46,"_75":604,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":3996,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4023,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4021,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4018,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4017,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4016,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1396,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4015},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4012},[4013],{"_73":4014,"_50":594},"Tripo AI · VAST","The official README explicitly says TripoSR was collaboratively developed by Tripo AI and Stability AI. The VAST-AI-Research organization links to tripo3d.ai. This shows Tripo/VAST as one verified co-developer, not as the sole author.",[109],[1334],[3534,3890,4019,4020],"Mesh","Prototype assets",[4022],{"_73":1352,"_50":594},"Uses LRM-style feed-forward reconstruction, with public code, pretrained models, and a demo. An input image becomes an exportable object mesh. It focuses on individual objects; hidden surfaces, topology, and game performance need additional work. It is not a complete scene or playable game generator.",[3534,3890,4019,4020],[166],[126],"resource:trellis","Generates meshes, Gaussians, and radiance fields from structured latent representations.",{"_44":201,"_1363":198,"_1361":126,"_71":1364,"_1362":4028,"_1357":4060,"_50":4048,"_81":4061,"_1338":4062,"_1333":4063,"_1330":4064,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1395},[4031,4032,4033,4034,4035,4036,4037,4038,4039,4040,4041,4042,4043,4044,4045],{"_71":46,"_75":198,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4028,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4060,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4058,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4055,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4052,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4051,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4050,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1396,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":1591,"_77":1592,"_73":1593,"_94":194,"_103":195,"_57":190,"_78":187},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4049},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4046},[4047],{"_73":2406,"_50":4048},"https://github.com/microsoft/TRELLIS","The official research repository is hosted by Microsoft's organization. The asset is from Microsoft's official brand page and identifies the organization rather than fabricating a TRELLIS project mark.",[109],[1334],[3534,4053,3537,4054],"Text-to-3D","Structured Latents",[4056],{"_73":1411,"_50":4057},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.01506",[4059],{"_73":1352,"_50":4048},"Decodes image or text inputs into several 3D representations. Official examples support textured GLB export and simplification. Conventional game asset pipelines mainly use its mesh branch; Gaussian and radiance field outputs do not themselves include usable collision, animation, or gameplay logic.",[4065],[3534,4053,3537,4054],[166],[126],{"_73":1411,"_50":4057},"resource:hunyuan3d-2","Turns reference images into geometry and textures for 3D asset pipelines.",{"_44":643,"_1363":640,"_1361":126,"_71":1364,"_1362":4067,"_1357":4109,"_50":4087,"_81":4110,"_1338":4111,"_1333":4112,"_1330":4113,"_1324":1369,"_1321":1395},[4070,4071,4072,4073,4074,4075,4076,4077,4078,4079,4080,4081,4082,4083,4084],{"_71":46,"_75":640,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4067,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4109,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4107,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4097,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4095,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4094,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4093,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1323,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":1591,"_77":1592,"_73":1593,"_94":4089,"_103":4090,"_57":4091,"_78":4092},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4088},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4085},[4086],{"_73":3438,"_50":4087},"https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hunyuan3D-2","The official model repository is owned by Tencent-Hunyuan. That organization links to hy.tencent.com. Use its actual brand image rather than an unrelated 3D icon.","/GameMap/media/demos/hunyuan3d-2.webp","Official Tencent Hunyuan3D 2.0 generation results showing cartoon character assets on a pink background","https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hunyuan3D-2#%EF%B8%8F-hunyuan3d-20","Tencent Hunyuan · Hunyuan3D 2.0",[109],[1334],[3534,4019,4096,3981],"Textures",[4098,4099,4100],{"_73":4105,"_50":4106},{"_73":4103,"_50":4104},{"_73":4101,"_50":4102},"2.0 license","https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hunyuan3D-2/blob/main/LICENSE","2.1 repository","https://github.com/Tencent-Hunyuan/Hunyuan3D-2.1","2.0 paper","https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.12202",[4108],{"_73":1352,"_50":4087},"The 2.0 pipeline generates shape with Hunyuan3D-DiT and textures the mesh with Hunyuan3D-Paint. It supports GLB and OBJ export and a Blender addon under a dedicated Tencent Hunyuan 3D 2.0 community license. The separate 2.1 release adds a PBR texture pipeline and training code. Topology, LOD, rigging, collision, runtime performance, and each version's terms still need game-pipeline checks.",[4114,4115,4116],[3534,4019,4096,3981],[166],[126],{"_73":4105,"_50":4106},{"_73":4103,"_50":4104},{"_73":4101,"_50":4102},"resource:godot-3d-asset-skill","godot-3d-asset-skill","Godot MCP 3D Asset Builder","Builds reusable stylized 3D assets with Godot geometry and validation workflows.","/resources/godot-3d-asset-skill/",{"_44":4118,"_1363":4119,"_1361":126,"_71":2297,"_1362":4120,"_1357":4150,"_50":4139,"_1338":4151,"_1333":4152,"_1330":4153,"_1321":1395},[4124,4125,4126,4127,4128,4129,4130,4131,4132,4133,4134,4135],{"_71":46,"_75":4119,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4120,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2318,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4150,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4148,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4143,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4142,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4141,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4140},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4136},[4137],{"_73":4138,"_50":4139},"LuigiDeFacci","https://github.com/LuigiDeFacci/godot-create-3d-assets","The public repository is independently maintained by LuigiDeFacci. Its image files are scene screenshots, with no project or institutional mark found. The account image is a default GitHub identicon, so it must not be used as a logo. Show the maintainer name without inventing an affiliation or reusing the Godot engine logo.",[109],[1334,1335,1545],[4144,4145,4146,4147],"Godot","Agent Skill","PackedScene","Asset QA",[4149],{"_73":1352,"_50":4139},"Takes project style and asset requirements, then uses Godot MCP and deterministic builders to produce PackedScene assets and check grounding, collision, navigation, and screenshots. Designed for Codex and Claude Code, it can reuse existing project resources. It requires compatible MCP capabilities and is not an image-to-mesh generative model.",[4144,4145,4146,4147],[166,1370,1562],[126],"resource:mcp-unity","mcp-unity","MCP Unity Editor","A community MCP bridge for querying, editing, and testing Unity projects.","/resources/mcp-unity/",{"_44":4155,"_1363":4156,"_1361":126,"_71":1364,"_1362":4157,"_1357":4186,"_50":4176,"_1338":4187,"_1333":4188,"_1330":4189,"_1321":1395},[4161,4162,4163,4164,4165,4166,4167,4168,4169,4170,4171,4172],{"_71":46,"_75":4156,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4157,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4186,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4184,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4180,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4179,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4178,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4177},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4173},[4174],{"_73":4175,"_50":4176},"Miguel Tomas · CoderGamester","https://github.com/CoderGamester/mcp-unity","The independent repository is maintained by CoderGamester, whose profile names Miguel Tomas. The file index has no project image mark and the README uses ASCII art and third-party badges. The maintainer avatar is a personal photograph, so it is not used as a brand logo. Do not attribute this third-party plugin to Unity or to the maintainer's employer.",[232,109],[1447,1335,1545],[3229,4181,4182,4183],"MCP","Editor automation","Community tool",[4185],{"_73":1352,"_50":4176},"Exposes scenes, GameObjects, components, Prefabs, logs, Unity Test Runner, and other editor operations to MCP clients. This community tool is separate from Unity's official plugin. Its README warns that entering Play Mode with domain reload can disconnect the bridge; check the installed version, test configuration, and actual results. Editor automation alone does not establish correct gameplay.",[3229,4181,4182,4183],[1470,1370,1562],[247,126],"resource:unity-agent-plugin","unity-agent-plugin","Unity Agent Plugin","Unity-maintained project skills give general coding agents engine-specific context.","/resources/unity-agent-plugin/",{"_44":4191,"_1363":4192,"_1361":126,"_71":2297,"_1362":4193,"_1357":4230,"_50":4213,"_81":4231,"_1338":4232,"_1333":4233,"_1330":4234,"_1321":1395},[4197,4198,4199,4200,4201,4202,4203,4204,4205,4206,4207,4208,4209],{"_71":46,"_75":4192,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4193,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2318,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4230,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4228,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4221,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4217,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4216,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4215,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4214},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4210},[4211],{"_73":4212,"_50":4213},"Unity Technologies","https://docs.unity.com/en-us/ai/unity-plugin/about-unity-plugin","Unity's own product documentation identifies the official plugin, with source under the Unity-Technologies organization. Use the official organization's brand image; this attribution applies to the official plugin, not independent Unity MCP bridges.",[232,109],[1637,1447,1335,1545,2294],[4218,4219,3229,4220,4181],"Official","Agent Skills","CLI",[4222,4223],{"_73":4226,"_50":4227},{"_73":4224,"_50":4225},"CLI / MCP migration","https://docs.unity.com/en-us/unity-cli/replace-mcp-server-unity-cli","Skill source","https://github.com/Unity-Technologies/unity-agent-plugin/tree/main/skills",[4229],{"_73":1352,"_50":4213},"Provides Claude Code, Codex, and Grok with skills for 2D, UI, rendering, navigation, physics, multiplayer, and other tasks, connected to Unity CLI and MCP controls. Unity requires version 6.0 or later. The current CLI MCP mode replaces MCP in the older assistant package; follow the documentation for the version in use.",[4235,4236],[4218,4219,3229,4220,4181],[1653,1470,1370,1562,2332],[247,126],{"_73":4226,"_50":4227},{"_73":4224,"_50":4225},"resource:gameenginebench","gameenginebench","GameEngineBench","Tests agent-written C++ runtime changes in real Unreal Engine projects.","/resources/gameenginebench/",{"_44":4238,"_1363":4239,"_1361":126,"_71":1722,"_1362":4240,"_1357":4279,"_50":4278,"_81":4281,"_1338":4282,"_1333":4283,"_1330":4284,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1395},[4244,4245,4246,4247,4248,4249,4250,4251,4252,4253,4254,4255,4256,4257],{"_71":46,"_75":4239,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4240,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4280,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4279,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4276,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4269,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4265,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4264,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4263,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4262},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4258},[4259],{"_73":4260,"_50":4261},"Nitrode","https://arxiv.org/html/2607.03525","The paper lists Brian La, Sejoon Chang, and Ben Kim at Nitrode, provides research@nitrode.com, and links the Nitrode-Research repository. Other affiliations include Nexon Intelligence Labs and several universities. The paper explicitly says authors' views do not necessarily reflect employer or institutional policy. The mark is linked from Nitrode's official site.",[109],[1447,1545],[4266,715,4267,4268],"Development benchmark","C++","Behavior tests",[4270,4271],{"_73":4274,"_50":4275},{"_73":4272,"_50":4273},"Versioned evaluation protocol","https://arxiv.org/html/2607.03525v2","Paper-linked repository (availability unverified)","https://github.com/Nitrode-Research/GameEngineBench",[4277],{"_73":1352,"_50":4278},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03525","Paper v2 describes 110 scoped C++ tasks from nine Unreal projects. Agents receive a buildable start, allowed files, and behavioral requirements. After compilation and Play-in-Editor listen-server tests, an LLM judge reviews the specification, test evidence, edits, and reference solution to determine success. The paper-linked repository could not be retrieved during review, so runnable-code availability remains unverified. The scope is local C++ implementation, not complete 3D game generation.","Benchmark",[4285,4286],[4266,715,4267,4268],[1470,1562],[126],{"_73":4274,"_50":4275},{"_73":4272,"_50":4273},"resource:gamefactory-3a","Coordinates game assets, gameplay, and UI through skills, model pipelines, and engine adapters.",{"_44":432,"_1363":428,"_1361":126,"_71":1465,"_1362":4288,"_1357":4321,"_50":4308,"_81":4322,"_1338":4323,"_1333":4324,"_1330":4325,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1395},[4291,4292,4293,4294,4295,4296,4297,4298,4299,4300,4301,4302,4303,4304],{"_71":46,"_75":428,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4288,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":3667,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4321,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4319,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4315,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4312,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4311,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4310,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4309},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4305},[4306],{"_73":4307,"_50":4308},"OpenDCAI","https://github.com/OpenDCAI/GameFactory-3A","The official repository is owned by the OpenDCAI organization, whose profile describes data-centric AI research. No university affiliation was established from the project or organization profile. Use only the organization's actual selected identity image; do not infer a school from the project name.",[232,109],[1637,1447,1334,1335,1545],[4219,4313,4314,3722],"Asset pipelines","Multiple engines",[4316],{"_73":4317,"_50":4318},"Chinese documentation","https://github.com/OpenDCAI/GameFactory-3A/blob/main/README_zh.md",[4320],{"_73":1352,"_50":4308},"A coding agent routes requirements through image, 3D, motion, audio, and other pipelines to produce assets and engine-native code, with context for UE5, Unity, Godot, Blender, and three.js. Demos mix generated and existing resources. The 3A name is not a verified commercial quality rating. This is a separate project from Kling's GameFactory video world model.",[4326],[4219,4313,4314,3722],[1653,1470,166,1370,1562],[247,126],{"_73":4317,"_50":4318},"resource:openai-image-api","openai-image-api","OpenAI Image Generation","Generate and edit raster art using image endpoints or a conversational image-generation tool.","/resources/openai-image-api/",{"_44":4328,"_1363":4329,"_1361":247,"_71":1364,"_1362":4330,"_1357":4355,"_50":4349,"_81":4357,"_1338":4358,"_1333":4359,"_1330":4360,"_1321":1395},[4334,4335,4336,4337,4338,4339,4340,4341,4342,4343,4344,4345],{"_71":46,"_75":4329,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4330,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4355,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4353,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4352,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4351,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4350,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":2361},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4346},[4347],{"_73":4348,"_50":4349},"OpenAI","https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/image-generation",[232,109],[1334],[3659],[4354],{"_73":1352,"_50":4349},"Generate or edit raster images through the Images API or multi-turn Responses workflows. Save output bytes and request settings; masks guide edits rather than guaranteeing exact boundaries. Sprite consistency and seamless textures need separate checks. The technical guide does not establish output rights or retry billing.","2D development",[],[3659],[166],[247,126],"resource:agent-sprite-forge","Combines reference art, generated animation, and deterministic processing into exportable sprites.",{"_44":679,"_1363":674,"_1361":247,"_71":2297,"_1362":4362,"_1357":4388,"_50":666,"_1338":4389,"_1333":4390,"_1330":4391,"_1321":1395},[4365,4366,4367,4368,4369,4370,4371,4372,4373,4374,4375,4376],{"_71":46,"_75":674,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4362,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2318,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4388,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4386,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4383,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4382,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4381,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4380},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4377},[4378],{"_73":4379,"_50":666},"0x0funky","Independent project maintained by 0x0funky. No separate public project logo or institutional affiliation is confirmed. The maintainer uses a custom illustrated profile avatar, which is omitted because it is not an official project or organization mark. The robot mark in Agent Game Forge belongs to a different project and is not reused here.",[232],[1334,1545],[4145,4384,4385,4147],"Sprite pipeline","Animation",[4387],{"_73":1352,"_50":666},"Generates motion clips from an approved reference image, then performs background removal, alignment, loop selection, timing correction, and atlas packaging. It offers Godot, Aseprite, and web exports. For 0.4.0, the README reports parse-level round trips but no Godot, LDtk, or Aseprite editor-import verification. Import and visual acceptance checks remain necessary.",[4145,4384,4385,4147],[166,1562],[247],"resource:pixellab","pixellab","PixelLab AI Agent Toolkit","Generates pixel characters, animation, and seamless tilesets through API and MCP tools.","/resources/pixellab/",{"_44":4393,"_1363":4394,"_1361":247,"_71":1364,"_1362":4395,"_1357":4428,"_50":4415,"_81":4429,"_1338":4430,"_1333":4431,"_1330":4432,"_1321":1395},[4399,4400,4401,4402,4403,4404,4405,4406,4407,4408,4409,4410,4411],{"_71":46,"_75":4394,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4395,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4428,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4426,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4423,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4419,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4418,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4417,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4416},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4412},[4413],{"_73":4414,"_50":4415},"PixelLab","https://www.pixellab.ai/mcp","The official PixelLab site describes its MCP asset service. The pixellab-code GitHub organization names itself PixelLab and links back to www.pixellab.ai; this is its official organization image, not a generated symbol.",[232],[1334,1335],[4420,4421,4422,4181,3161],"Pixel art","Sprite","Tileset",[4424],{"_73":2528,"_50":4425},"https://www.pixellab.ai/docs",[4427],{"_73":1352,"_50":4415},"Accepts character descriptions, directions, actions, and terrain conditions to produce pixel assets, including four- or eight-direction characters and side-view or top-down tilesets. This is a commercial asset service. MCP connects its asset tools to coding agents; game rules, collision, and asset import still require a project workflow.",[4433],[4420,4421,4422,4181,3161],[166,1370],[247],{"_73":2528,"_50":4425},"resource:text2game","text2game","Text2Game","Turns long-form text into world, character, and event data for narrative prototypes.","/resources/text2game/",{"_44":4435,"_1363":4436,"_1361":247,"_71":1364,"_1362":4437,"_1357":4466,"_50":4456,"_1338":4467,"_1333":4468,"_1330":4469,"_1321":1395},[4441,4442,4443,4444,4445,4446,4447,4448,4449,4450,4451,4452],{"_71":46,"_75":4436,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4437,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4466,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4464,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4460,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4459,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4458,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4457},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4453},[4454],{"_73":4455,"_50":4456},"Song Li · boltomli","https://github.com/boltomli/t2g","The public repository is maintained under boltomli, whose GitHub profile names Song Li. Its README and file index expose no project or institutional brand mark. The profile image is a toy photograph and is not used as a logo. Show the verified maintainer name without inventing a school or company mark.",[232],[1637,1447,1335],[4461,4462,4144,4463],"Interactive narrative","Twine","Visual novels",[4465],{"_73":1352,"_50":4456},"Analyzes text in chunks, merges the results, and generates Twine/Chapbook HTML or Godot visual novel projects. The repository provides a Python pipeline and examples for research on turning narratives into playable prototypes. It offers no general guarantee of generating arbitrary action games.",[4461,4462,4144,4463],[1653,1470,1370],[247],"resource:agent-game-forge","agent-game-forge","Agent Game Forge","A local 2D game IDE with a scene editor for Codex and Claude Code.","/resources/agent-game-forge/",{"_44":4471,"_1363":4472,"_1361":247,"_71":1364,"_1362":4473,"_1357":4503,"_50":4492,"_1338":4504,"_1333":4505,"_1330":4506,"_1321":1395},[4477,4478,4479,4480,4481,4482,4483,4484,4485,4486,4487,4488],{"_71":46,"_75":4472,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4473,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4503,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4501,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4496,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4495,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4494,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4493},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4489},[4490],{"_73":4491,"_50":4492},"Agent Game Forge · 0x0funky","https://github.com/0x0funky/agent-game-forge","This is the actual project logo committed in the official repository's web/public directory, with several size variants. The repository is independently maintained by 0x0funky; no university or corporate affiliation is asserted.",[232],[1637,1447,1334,1335,1545,2294],[4497,4498,4499,4500],"2D IDE","Canvas","Scene editing","Prototyping",[4502],{"_73":1352,"_50":4492},"Agents, asset workflows, and JSON scene data turn natural-language requests into JS + Canvas games. Users can adjust layout and collision in a visual editor. The README lists web output as the current default, with full Godot and Unity support still on the roadmap. The project describes itself as pre-launch.",[4497,4498,4499,4500],[1653,1470,166,1370,1562,2332],[247],"resource:cardiverse","cardiverse","Cardiverse","Connects card game design, Python rule code, and playtesting in a prototype pipeline.","/resources/cardiverse/",{"_44":4508,"_1363":4509,"_1361":247,"_71":1465,"_1362":4510,"_1357":4546,"_50":4545,"_81":4547,"_1338":4548,"_1333":4549,"_1330":4550,"_1324":1369,"_1321":1395},[4514,4515,4516,4517,4518,4519,4520,4521,4522,4523,4524,4525,4526,4527],{"_71":46,"_75":4509,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4510,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4546,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4543,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4540,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4535,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4534,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4533,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1323,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4532},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4528},[4529],{"_73":4530,"_50":4531},"Rutgers University","https://arxiv.org/html/2502.07128","The paper lists first author Danrui Li and several coauthors at Rutgers, with other affiliations including Ontario Tech and Roblox. The SVG is linked from Rutgers' official Logos, Signatures, and Visual Identity page. This is a representative author affiliation.",[232],[1637,1447,1545],[4536,4537,4538,4539],"Card games","Mechanism graphs","Code generation","Self-play validation",[4541],{"_73":1411,"_50":4542},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.07128",[4544],{"_73":1352,"_50":4545},"https://github.com/danruili/Cardiverse","Uses mechanism graphs and retrieval to generate variants and code from card game descriptions, then iteratively checks rule consistency using generated match records. The repository also includes a gameplay AI arena, but its development contribution centers on rule and code prototypes. Public substitute rule descriptions differ from the original paper inputs, which affects reproducibility.",[4551],[4536,4537,4538,4539],[1653,1470,1562],[247],{"_73":1411,"_50":4542},"resource:gavel","gavel","GAVEL","Combines language models and quality-diversity search to create board game rules.","/resources/gavel/",{"_44":4553,"_1363":4554,"_1361":247,"_71":1465,"_1362":4555,"_1357":4591,"_50":4590,"_81":4592,"_1338":4593,"_1333":4594,"_1330":4595,"_1324":1417,"_1321":1395},[4559,4560,4561,4562,4563,4564,4565,4566,4567,4568,4569,4570,4571,4572],{"_71":46,"_75":4554,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4555,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4591,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4588,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4585,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4580,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4579,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4578,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1396,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4577},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4573},[4574],{"_73":4575,"_50":4576},"New York University · Tandon School of Engineering","https://arxiv.org/html/2407.09388","The paper lists first author Graham Todd and Julian Togelius at NYU Tandon. Other authors list ETH Zurich, Flinders, UCLouvain, and Maastricht. This identifies the first author's institution using NYU Tandon's own website icon.",[232],[1637,1447,1545],[4581,4582,4583,4584],"Game design","Ludii","Evolutionary search","Rule generation",[4586],{"_73":1411,"_50":4587},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.09388",[4589],{"_73":1352,"_50":4590},"https://github.com/gdrtodd/gavel","Uses Ludii game description code as its representation. A language model mutates and recombines rules, then simulation and search select games. Code, experiments, and related model and data references are public. The outputs are board games within a rule system; these results do not establish general 2D action game development ability.",[4596],[4581,4582,4583,4584],[1653,1470,1562],[247],{"_73":1411,"_50":4587},"resource:mariogpt","mariogpt","MarioGPT","Generates playable Mario-style level layouts from text with a GPT model.","/resources/mariogpt/",{"_44":4598,"_1363":4599,"_1361":247,"_71":1412,"_1362":4600,"_1357":4640,"_50":4626,"_81":4641,"_1338":4642,"_1333":4643,"_1330":4644,"_1324":3951,"_1321":1395},[4604,4605,4606,4607,4608,4609,4610,4611,4612,4613,4614,4615,4616,4617,4618],{"_71":46,"_75":4599,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4600,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1411,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4640,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4638,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4635,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4630,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4629,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4628,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":3932,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":1591,"_77":1592,"_73":1593,"_94":4624,"_103":4625,"_57":4626,"_78":4627},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4623},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4619},[4620],{"_73":4621,"_50":4622},"IT University of Copenhagen","https://arxiv.org/html/2302.05981","The paper lists first author Shyam Sudhakaran at IT University of Copenhagen and modl.ai; other authors also list ITU and modl.ai. Uses the university's official English logo. This is one verified affiliation rather than exclusive institutional authorship.","/GameMap/media/demos/mariogpt.webp","First frame of the official MarioGPT interactive demo, showing a Mario-style platform level","https://github.com/shyamsn97/mario-gpt","MarioGPT authors · official demo still",[232],[1637,1335,1545],[4631,4632,4633,4634],"PCG","Level generation","Text-to-level","GPT-2",[4636],{"_73":1411,"_50":4637},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.05981",[4639],{"_73":1352,"_50":4626},"Descriptions of enemies, pipes, and elevation become character-grid levels and previews, with an interactive simulator or A* checks available. It generates level content within existing rules and supports research on controllable procedural content generation. Its scope does not include game engines, character art, or complete gameplay code.",[4645],[4631,4632,4633,4634],[1653,1370,1562],[247],{"_73":1411,"_50":4637},"resource:gamegen-verifier","gamegen-verifier","GameGen-Verifier","Verifies generated game behavior through runtime state hooks and focused checks.","/resources/gamegen-verifier/",{"_44":4647,"_1363":4648,"_1361":247,"_71":1465,"_1362":4649,"_1357":4685,"_50":4684,"_81":4686,"_1338":4687,"_1333":4688,"_1330":4689,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1395},[4653,4654,4655,4656,4657,4658,4659,4660,4661,4662,4663,4664,4665,4666],{"_71":46,"_75":4648,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4649,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4685,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4682,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4679,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4674,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4673,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4672,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4671},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4667},[4668],{"_73":4669,"_50":4670},"The Chinese University of Hong Kong","https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.07442","The PDF's first page assigns first author Chaobo Jia and Hong Xu to affiliation 1, CUHK. Equal contributors and coauthors also list HUST, Lionrock AI Lab, NTU, HKU, and an independent researcher. The university icon identifies one verified author affiliation, not the sole project owner.",[232,109],[1447,1545],[4675,4676,4677,4678],"Functional verification","Playwright","Runtime state","Verifier Skill",[4680],{"_73":1411,"_50":4681},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.07442",[4683],{"_73":1352,"_50":4684},"https://github.com/NetX-lab/GameGen-Verifier","Breaks game requirements into independently testable checkpoints and checks functionality through browser and runtime adapters. The repository provides GGV-Harness and verifier skills for Codex and Claude. Public code does not include all generated games, run outputs, or private configurations. State hooks also provide observability beyond a purely black-box playtest.",[4690],[4675,4676,4677,4678],[1470,1562],[247,126],{"_73":1411,"_50":4681},"resource:gamexpert-bench","gamexpert-bench","GameXpert-Bench","Benchmarks game creation, bug fixing, and iterative improvement in three tracks.","/resources/gamexpert-bench/",{"_44":4692,"_1363":4693,"_1361":247,"_71":1722,"_1362":4694,"_1357":4730,"_50":4729,"_81":4731,"_1338":4732,"_1333":4733,"_1330":4734,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1395},[4698,4699,4700,4701,4702,4703,4704,4705,4706,4707,4708,4709,4710,4711],{"_71":46,"_75":4693,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4694,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4280,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4730,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4727,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4723,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4719,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4718,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4717,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4716},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4712},[4713],{"_73":4714,"_50":4715},"Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences","https://arxiv.org/html/2608.21833","The paper lists first author Kun Chen at MAIS, Institute of Automation, Chinese Academy of Sciences. It also lists Tsinghua, HKUST, CUHK Shenzhen, Tencent Lightspeed Studios, and the Tencent Hunyuan team. The institute icon is linked by its official identity page https://ia.cas.cn/gkjj/xxbs/. Affiliation is representative, not exclusive.",[232,109],[1637,1447,1545],[4266,4720,4721,4722],"Bug fixing","Iterative improvement","Full release pending",[4724],{"_73":4725,"_50":4726},"Repository and release status","https://github.com/Kwen-Chen/GameXpert-Bench",[4728],{"_73":1352,"_50":4729},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.21833","The paper introduces GameGen, GameFix, and GameOpt using complete development trajectories to study the lifecycle beyond a single generation. At review, the official repository still said data and evaluation code were being prepared for release. Treat it as a paper and protocol reference, not a ready-to-run benchmark.",[4735],[4266,4720,4721,4722],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126],{"_73":4725,"_50":4726},"resource:gamedevbench","gamedevbench","GameDevBench","Evaluates coding agents on development tasks in existing Godot projects.","/resources/gamedevbench/",{"_44":4737,"_1363":4738,"_1361":247,"_71":1722,"_1362":4739,"_1357":4773,"_50":4772,"_81":4774,"_1338":4775,"_1333":4776,"_1330":4777,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1395},[4743,4744,4745,4746,4747,4748,4749,4750,4751,4752,4753,4754,4755,4756],{"_71":46,"_75":4738,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4739,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4280,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4773,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4770,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4767,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4764,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4763,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4762,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4761},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4757},[4758],{"_73":4759,"_50":4760},"Carnegie Mellon University","https://arxiv.org/html/2602.11103","The paper lists first author Wayne Chi and most coauthors at Carnegie Mellon; one coauthor is at Princeton. This represents the first author's affiliation, not a claim of exclusive authorship. The 900px square logo is the image displayed on CMU's official brand standards University Logo page.",[232,109],[1447,1335,1545],[4266,4144,4765,4766],"Multimodal","Visual feedback",[4768],{"_73":1411,"_50":4769},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.11103",[4771],{"_73":1352,"_50":4772},"https://github.com/waynchi/gamedevbench","The repository contains 333 tasks across 2D, 3D, UI, and gameplay logic. Agents receive an existing project and a task, then produce changes that can be checked in the engine. Comparable official runs require Godot 4.4.1 and provide image or video feedback. This measures bounded development tasks, not the quality of commercial games created from scratch.",[4778],[4266,4144,4765,4766],[1470,1370,1562],[247,126],{"_73":1411,"_50":4769},"resource:opengame","Generates browser game projects with reusable templates and debugging skills.",{"_44":250,"_1363":235,"_1361":247,"_71":4817,"_1362":4780,"_1357":4815,"_50":4801,"_81":4818,"_1338":4819,"_1333":4820,"_1330":4821,"_1324":1951,"_1321":1395},[4783,4784,4785,4786,4787,4788,4789,4790,4791,4792,4793,4794,4795,4796,4797],{"_71":46,"_75":235,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4780,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4816,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4815,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4813,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4810,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4806,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4805,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4804,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":1926,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":1591,"_77":1592,"_73":1593,"_94":230,"_103":231,"_57":4803,"_78":223},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4802},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4798},[4799],{"_73":4800,"_50":4801},"The Chinese University of Hong Kong · MMLab","https://github.com/leigest519/OpenGame","The official README directly identifies the author team as CUHK MMLab and lists CUHK email addresses. Uses the university's official website icon to identify that affiliation.","https://github.com/leigest519/OpenGame#playable-demos",[232,109],[1637,1447,1334,1545],[2761,4807,4808,4809],"Game Skill","Browser feedback","GameCoder-27B",[4811],{"_73":1411,"_50":4812},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.18394",[4814],{"_73":1352,"_50":4801},"Turns natural-language requirements into web projects using Template Skill and Debug Skill for Canvas, Phaser, three.js, and other templates. The public CLI accepts OpenAI-compatible model endpoints; the paper also introduces GameCoder-27B. Browser execution and visual judging assess build health, usability, and intent alignment. The README still lists the standalone evaluation pipeline as forthcoming; model weights and full evaluation reproducibility are not established by the framework release alone.","Agent","agent",[4822],[2761,4807,4808,4809],[1653,1470,166,1562],[247,126],{"_73":1411,"_50":4812},"resource:gamegpt","gamegpt","GameGPT","Studies automated game development through multi-agent planning and code generation.","/resources/gamegpt/",{"_44":4824,"_1363":4825,"_1361":247,"_71":1412,"_1362":4826,"_1357":4860,"_50":4859,"_81":4861,"_1338":4862,"_1333":4863,"_1330":4864,"_1324":3951,"_1321":1395},[4830,4831,4832,4833,4834,4835,4836,4837,4838,4839,4840,4841,4842,4843],{"_71":46,"_75":4825,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4826,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4356,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1411,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4860,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4857,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4853,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4851,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4850,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4849,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1322,"_75":3932,"_77":1324,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4848},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4844},[4845],{"_73":4846,"_50":4847},"AutoGame Research","https://arxiv.org/html/2310.08067","The paper lists first author Dake Chen at AutoGame Research and uses autogame.ai email addresses for other AutoGame authors. The logo is linked by AutoGame's official homepage. Other author affiliations include X-Institute, USC, and Tsinghua; this is a representative research affiliation, not exclusive ownership or endorsement.",[232,109],[1637,1447,1545],[3784,4852,3724],"Task planning",[4854],{"_73":4855,"_50":4856},"Paper and README repository","https://github.com/leyiwo/GameGPT",[4858],{"_73":1352,"_50":4859},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.08067","Planning, review, and implementation agents break down game requirements and generate code, with a focus on hallucination and redundancy. This is an early research framework for game development agents. The linked repository contains only the paper and README; it is not a verified, ready-to-deploy product.",[4865],[3784,4852,3724],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126],{"_73":4855,"_50":4856},"resource:unity-addressables-scripting","unity-addressables-scripting","Unity · Addressables Build and Loading APIs","Builds addressable content from explicit profiles and loads assets through asynchronous handles.","/resources/unity-addressables-scripting/",{"_44":4867,"_1363":4868,"_1361":4904,"_71":2529,"_1362":4869,"_1357":4902,"_50":4888,"_81":4905,"_1338":4906,"_1333":4907,"_1330":4908,"_1321":1395},[4873,4874,4875,4876,4877,4878,4879,4880,4881,4882,4883,4884,4885],{"_71":46,"_75":4868,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4869,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4903,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2528,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4902,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4900,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4896,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4891,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4890,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4889,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":2641},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4886},[4887],{"_73":3229,"_50":4888},"https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.addressables@1.21/manual/build-scripting-start-build.html",[232,109],[1334,1447,2294,3085],[3229,4892,4893,4894,4895],"Addressables","Asset dependencies","Async loading","Content builds",[4897],{"_73":4898,"_50":4899},"LoadAssetAsync reference","https://docs.unity3d.com/kr/Packages/com.unity.addressables%401.21/api/UnityEngine.AddressableAssets.Addressables.LoadAssetAsync.html",[4901],{"_73":1352,"_50":4888},"The checked Addressables 1.21 documentation separates content builds from executable builds. Build settings, active profile, builder, and content-state file affect outputs. Runtime loading returns a handle whose status and result must be checked and later released. A key matching several assets can select only the first; preserve dependency and cache provenance.","Engines & creation tools","engines",[4909],[3229,4892,4893,4894,4895],[166,1470,2332,3108],[247,126],{"_73":4898,"_50":4899},"resource:unreal-remote-control","unreal-remote-control","Unreal Engine · Remote Control API","Exposes reflected editor properties and functions over HTTP for external tooling.","/resources/unreal-remote-control/",{"_44":4911,"_1363":4912,"_1361":4904,"_71":2529,"_1362":4913,"_1357":4944,"_50":4932,"_81":4945,"_1338":4946,"_1333":4947,"_1330":4948,"_1321":1395},[4917,4918,4919,4920,4921,4922,4923,4924,4925,4926,4927,4928,4929],{"_71":46,"_75":4912,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4913,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4903,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2528,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4944,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4942,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":4938,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4935,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4934,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4933,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":2641},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4930},[4931],{"_73":2698,"_50":4932},"https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/remote-control-for-unreal-engine",[109],[1447,1335,1545],[715,4936,4182,4937],"HTTP","State mutation",[4939],{"_73":4940,"_50":4941},"HTTP API reference","https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/remote-control-api-http-reference-for-unreal-engine",[4943],{"_73":1352,"_50":4932},"Remote Control provides a native engine integration surface distinct from a community MCP bridge. Property writes can request editor transactions and change notifications, but an acknowledged mutation does not establish package-save completion. The rolling Epic guide labels this feature Beta and disables it by default in packaged builds and -game. Enable the appropriate plugin, restrict network exposure, and qualify editor versus packaged-runtime access separately.",[4949],[715,4936,4182,4937],[1470,1370,1562],[126],{"_73":4940,"_50":4941},"resource:phaser-examples","phaser-examples","Phaser · Examples","Official Phaser example source with runnable references for specific APIs and gameplay components.","/resources/phaser-examples/",{"_44":4951,"_1363":4952,"_1361":4904,"_71":2529,"_1362":4953,"_1357":4984,"_50":4983,"_1338":4985,"_1333":4986,"_1330":4987,"_1321":1395},[4957,4958,4959,4960,4961,4962,4963,4964,4965,4966,4967,4968],{"_71":46,"_75":4952,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4953,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4903,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2528,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":4984,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":4981,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":4976,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":4975,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":4974,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":4973},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":4969},[4970],{"_73":4971,"_50":4972},"Phaser / Phaser Studio","https://github.com/phaserjs/phaser","Official framework and examples organization. README explicitly attributes Phaser logo and characters to Phaser Studio Inc. The organization avatar avoids using a version-4 wordmark on Phaser-3 examples.",[232],[1447,1335,1545],[4977,4978,4979,232,4980],"Phaser","Official examples","Runnable source","Version scope",[4982],{"_73":1352,"_50":4983},"https://github.com/phaserjs/examples","Official examples for animation, cameras, input, physics, and scene transitions. The current README targets Phaser 4, and the labs site defaults to its latest development build; select and pin the version matching your project. The MIT license covers example code, not bundled art assets. Review asset permissions before reuse and test in a real browser.",[4977,4978,4979,232,4980],[1470,1370,1562],[247],"resource:phaser","A browser 2D game framework whose official tutorial covers assets, scenes, animation, input, and collisions.",{"_44":1059,"_1363":1051,"_1361":4904,"_71":1364,"_1362":4989,"_1357":5021,"_50":5020,"_81":5022,"_1338":5023,"_1333":5024,"_1330":5025,"_1321":1395},[4992,4993,4994,4995,4996,4997,4998,4999,5000,5001,5002,5003,5004],{"_71":46,"_75":1051,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":4989,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":4903,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1359,"_77":