ttps://agentskills.io/home","The official format website states Agent Skills was originally developed by Anthropic. Label as creator; the open format is adopted across the ecosystem.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1334,1335,1545,2294],[6075,6186,6187,6188],"Open format","Workflows","Progressive loading",[6190],{"_73":1352,"_50":6181},"Useful for repeatable game tasks such as sprite normalization, GLB export, scene inspection, and regression testing, with domain knowledge loaded as needed. Skills provide procedures and resources; engine control still requires tools, dependencies, and a compatible client.",[6075,6186,6187,6188],[1653,1470,166,1370,1562,2332],[247,126,293],"resource:agents-md","agents-md","AGENTS.md","An open Markdown format for giving coding agents build commands, test rules, and project conventions.","/resources/agents-md/",{"_44":6196,"_1363":6197,"_1361":5913,"_71":2529,"_1362":6198,"_1357":6226,"_50":6217,"_1338":6227,"_1333":6228,"_1330":6229,"_1321":1395},[6202,6203,6204,6205,6206,6207,6208,6209,6210,6211,6212,6213],{"_71":46,"_75":6197,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6198,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2528,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6226,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6224,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6221,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6220,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6219,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6218},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6214},[6215],{"_73":6216,"_50":6217},"Agentic AI Foundation","https://agents.md/","AGENTS.md explicitly states current stewardship by the Agentic AI Foundation under the Linux Foundation. Logo is the AAIF author mark used on aaif.io, not an OpenAI ownership claim.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545,2294],[6222,6223,6186,5104],"Project instructions","Project conventions",[6225],{"_73":1352,"_50":6217},"Game projects can record engine versions, launch commands, directory rules, asset import conventions, and acceptance checks to reduce environment guesswork. This is a project instruction format rather than an agent runtime; discovery and configuration vary by client.",[6222,6223,6186,5104],[1653,1470,1562,2332],[247,126,293],"resource:mini-swe-agent","mini-swe-agent","A minimal shell-based coding-agent research baseline designed for modification and trace inspection.","/resources/mini-swe-agent/",{"_44":6231,"_1363":6231,"_1361":5913,"_71":1465,"_1362":6232,"_1357":6268,"_50":6267,"_81":6269,"_1338":6270,"_1333":6271,"_1330":6272,"_1321":1395},[6236,6237,6238,6239,6240,6241,6242,6243,6244,6245,6246,6247,6248],{"_71":46,"_75":6231,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6232,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6268,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6265,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6261,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6256,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6255,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6254,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6253},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6249},[6250],{"_73":6251,"_50":6252},"mini-SWE-agent / SWE-agent","https://github.com/SWE-agent/mini-swe-agent/blob/main/mkdocs.yml","The official MkDocs configuration explicitly sets assets/mini_square.svg as both logo and favicon. Prefer the actual project mark over assigning one university from a multi-institution team.",[232,109,286],[1447,1545],[6257,6258,6259,6260,5144],"Research baseline","Shell","Harness","Traces",[6262],{"_73":6263,"_50":6264},"Predecessor: SWE-agent","https://github.com/SWE-agent/SWE-agent",[6266],{"_73":1352,"_50":6267},"https://github.com/SWE-agent/mini-swe-agent","Useful for isolating model, prompt, and environment effects in game code generation and repair, or wrapping headless engine commands. Its minimal loop executes commands in independent subprocesses rather than a persistent shell, so working-directory and environment setup must be carried into each command or script. It is a general software-engineering baseline; playability, visuals, and physics require additional validation.",[6273],[6257,6258,6259,6260,5144],[1470,1562],[247,126,293],{"_73":6263,"_50":6264},"resource:claude-agent-sdk","claude-agent-sdk","Claude Agent SDK","Embed Claude Code's tool loop, permissions, sessions, and extensions in Python or TypeScript applications.","/resources/claude-agent-sdk/",{"_44":6275,"_1363":6276,"_1361":5913,"_71":1465,"_1362":6277,"_1357":6306,"_50":6305,"_1338":6307,"_1333":6308,"_1330":6309,"_1321":1395},[6281,6282,6283,6284,6285,6286,6287,6288,6289,6290,6291,6292],{"_71":46,"_75":6276,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6277,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6306,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6303,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6299,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6298,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6297,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6296},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6293},[6294],{"_73":6180,"_50":6295},"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code","Official Anthropic product and SDK. The organization avatar is an official corporate mark.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545],[6300,5102,6301,4181,6302],"SDK","TypeScript","Hooks",[6304],{"_73":1352,"_50":6305},"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/overview","Runs the Claude Code binary and tool loop inside a process you operate, with Python or TypeScript APIs for permissions, sessions, hooks, and MCP. It can support game-specific repair and validation services, but domain tools, scoring rules, and runtime environments must be supplied. This differs from a Client SDK for direct model calls; the official overview also specifies Anthropic Commercial Terms and separate authentication constraints.",[6300,5102,6301,4181,6302],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126,293],"resource:openhands-sdk","openhands-sdk","OpenHands Software Agent SDK","A programmable development framework for agents, tools, conversations, workspaces, and server interfaces.","/resources/openhands-sdk/",{"_44":6311,"_1363":6312,"_1361":5913,"_71":1465,"_1362":6313,"_1357":6350,"_50":6349,"_81":6351,"_1338":6352,"_1333":6353,"_1330":6354,"_1321":1320},[6317,6318,6319,6320,6321,6322,6323,6324,6325,6326,6327,6328,6329],{"_71":46,"_75":6312,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6313,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6350,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6347,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6340,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6337,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6336,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6335,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1320,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6334},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6330},[6331],{"_73":6332,"_50":6333},"OpenHands","https://github.com/OpenHands/OpenHands","Official OpenHands README logo; the Software Agent SDK is maintained in the same OpenHands organization.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545],[6300,5102,6301,6338,6339],"Workspaces","Reproducible experiments",[6341,6342],{"_73":6345,"_50":6346},{"_73":6343,"_50":6344},"TypeScript client scope and stability","https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/blob/3f3294581ebf40f3bbe5b96aec1d28b7fec96226/clients/typescript/README.md#L1-L19","SDK documentation","https://docs.openhands.dev/sdk",[6348],{"_73":1352,"_50":6349},"https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk","Useful for wrapping builds, scene inspections, and tests as agent tools. The Python SDK supports local and remote workspaces; the checked TypeScript client is alpha and supports remote conversations through Agent Server only. Pin client/server versions rather than assuming interface parity. Game-specific tools and acceptance checks still need to be supplied.",[6355,6356],[6300,5102,6301,6338,6339],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126,293],{"_73":6345,"_50":6346},{"_73":6343,"_50":6344},"resource:openhands","openhands","OpenHands · Agent Canvas","An open-source development console for managing local, remote, and cloud agent environments.","/resources/openhands/",{"_44":6358,"_1363":6359,"_1361":5913,"_71":1465,"_1362":6360,"_1357":6390,"_50":6333,"_81":6391,"_1338":6392,"_1333":6393,"_1330":6394,"_1321":1395},[6364,6365,6366,6367,6368,6369,6370,6371,6372,6373,6374,6375,6376],{"_71":46,"_75":6359,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6360,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":1464,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6390,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6388,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6385,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6381,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6380,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6379,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6334},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6377},[6378],{"_73":6332,"_50":6333},[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545,2294],[6382,6383,3784,5144,6384],"Agent Canvas","Environments","Orchestration",[6386],{"_73":6387,"_50":6349},"Core SDK",[6389],{"_73":1352,"_50":6333},"Can centralize multi-agent tasks, environments, and execution records for game projects. The repository provides the Agent Canvas frontend and orchestration entry point; the core tool loop and Agent Server live in a separate SDK repository. Game automation still requires engine tools.",[6395],[6382,6383,3784,5144,6384],[1653,1470,1562,2332],[247,126,293],{"_73":6387,"_50":6349},"resource:aider","aider","Aider","A terminal AI pair-programming tool built around repository maps, Git changes, and lint and test feedback.","/resources/aider/",{"_44":6397,"_1363":6398,"_1361":5913,"_71":4817,"_1362":6399,"_1357":6436,"_50":6418,"_81":6437,"_1338":6438,"_1333":6439,"_1330":6440,"_1321":1320},[6403,6404,6405,6406,6407,6408,6409,6410,6411,6412,6413,6414,6415],{"_71":46,"_75":6398,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6399,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4816,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6436,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6434,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6427,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6422,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6421,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6420,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1320,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6419},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6416},[6417],{"_73":6398,"_50":6418},"https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider","Exact logo linked by the official project README.",[232,109,286],[1447,1545],[4220,6423,6424,6425,6426],"Git","Repository map","Multiple models","Refactoring",[6428,6429],{"_73":6432,"_50":6433},{"_73":6430,"_50":6431},"Screenshot and image input","https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider/blob/5dc9490bb35f9729ef2c95d00a19ccd30c26339c/aider/website/docs/usage/images-urls.md#L11-L27","User documentation","https://aider.chat/docs/",[6435],{"_73":1352,"_50":6418},"Useful for changes across files, refactoring, and testable logic in existing game projects, with model options including DeepSeek. It accepts supplied screenshots with a vision-capable model. Its code editing workflow does not directly control Unity, UE, or Blender editors; automated screenshot capture and game interaction need a separate setup.",[6441,6442],[4220,6423,6424,6425,6426],[1470,1562],[247,126,293],{"_73":6432,"_50":6433},{"_73":6430,"_50":6431},"resource:cline","cline","Cline","An open-source coding agent with multiple models, Plan / Act modes, project rules, and MCP support.","/resources/cline/",{"_44":6444,"_1363":6445,"_1361":5913,"_71":4817,"_1362":6446,"_1357":6477,"_50":6465,"_81":6478,"_1338":6479,"_1333":6480,"_1330":6481,"_1321":1395},[6450,6451,6452,6453,6454,6455,6456,6457,6458,6459,6460,6461,6462],{"_71":46,"_75":6445,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6446,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4816,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6477,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6475,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6472,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6469,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6468,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6467,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6466},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6463},[6464],{"_73":6445,"_50":6465},"https://github.com/cline/cline","Exact Cline project icon referenced at the top of the official README.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545],[6470,4220,6425,4181,6471],"IDE","Plan / Act",[6473],{"_73":2528,"_50":6474},"https://docs.cline.bot/",[6476],{"_73":1352,"_50":6465},"Useful for reviewing and editing game code in an IDE or CLI, with build output and MCP editor tools in the feedback loop. Reuse .clinerules and skills to capture engine conventions; editor operations depend on the specific bridge service.",[6482],[6470,4220,6425,4181,6471],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126,293],{"_73":2528,"_50":6474},"resource:opencode","opencode","OpenCode","An open-source coding agent with multiple model providers, Plan / Build modes, and project instructions.","/resources/opencode/",{"_44":6484,"_1363":6485,"_1361":5913,"_71":4817,"_1362":6486,"_1357":6520,"_50":6519,"_81":6521,"_1338":6522,"_1333":6523,"_1330":6524,"_1321":1395},[6490,6491,6492,6493,6494,6495,6496,6497,6498,6499,6500,6501,6502],{"_71":46,"_75":6485,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6486,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4816,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6520,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6517,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6512,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6510,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6509,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6508,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6507},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6503},[6504],{"_73":6505,"_50":6506},"OpenCode / Anomaly","https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode","Exact OpenCode logo referenced by the official README; use an appropriate light/dark variant without redrawing it.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545],[4220,6425,6511,5144,6197],"Plan / Build",[6513,6514],{"_73":5198,"_50":6506},{"_73":6515,"_50":6516},"V1 to V2 migration boundaries","https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/migrate-v1/",[6518],{"_73":1352,"_50":6519},"https://opencode.ai/docs/","Useful for planning and editing game projects with independently selected providers and models. Pin V1 or V2: the V2 migration guide documents incompatible plugin/server APIs, external-directory access allowed by default, and no running LSP or LSP diagnostics despite accepted configuration. Validate permissions, MCP integrations, and compiler/test feedback for the chosen version; editor and gameplay inspection still require separate tools.",[6525,6526],[4220,6425,6511,5144,6197],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126,293],{"_73":5198,"_50":6506},{"_73":6515,"_50":6516},"resource:deepseek-agent-integrations","deepseek-agent-integrations","DeepSeek · Agent Integrations","Official guidance for using DeepSeek as a model backend within agent harnesses such as Claude Code.","/resources/deepseek-agent-integrations/",{"_44":6528,"_1363":6529,"_1361":5913,"_71":2529,"_1362":6530,"_1357":6560,"_50":6559,"_1338":6561,"_1333":6562,"_1330":6563,"_1321":1395},[6534,6535,6536,6537,6538,6539,6540,6541,6542,6543,6544,6545],{"_71":46,"_75":6529,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6530,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":2528,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6560,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6557,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6553,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6552,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6551,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6550},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6546},[6547],{"_73":6548,"_50":6549},"DeepSeek","https://github.com/deepseek-ai","Official DeepSeek organization links its API documentation. This entry covers a model integration guide, not a separate game agent.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545],[6548,6554,6259,6555,6556],"Model backend","API compatibility","Scope",[6558],{"_73":1352,"_50":6559},"https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/anthropic_api/","The Anthropic API compatibility layer connects DeepSeek to existing tool loops. The harness handles files, tests, and engine connections. The guide supports ordinary tool calls but ignores the server-side mcp_servers field and does not support MCP-specific content blocks. Client-side MCP tools therefore remain the harness's responsibility; API compatibility does not establish complete feature parity.",[6548,6554,6259,6555,6556],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126,293],"resource:gemini-cli","gemini-cli","Gemini CLI","Google's open-source terminal coding agent with file access, shell tools, extensions, and MCP support.","/resources/gemini-cli/",{"_44":6565,"_1363":6566,"_1361":5913,"_71":4817,"_1362":6567,"_1357":6599,"_50":6587,"_81":6600,"_1338":6601,"_1333":6602,"_1330":6603,"_1321":1395},[6571,6572,6573,6574,6575,6576,6577,6578,6579,6580,6581,6582,6583],{"_71":46,"_75":6566,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6567,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4816,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6599,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6597,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6594,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6591,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6590,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6589,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6588},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6584},[6585],{"_73":6586,"_50":6587},"Google Gemini","https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli","Official Google Gemini project organization; the Gemini mark represents the product brand.",[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545],[4220,6592,4181,5144,6593],"Google","Migration guidance",[6595],{"_73":5015,"_50":6596},"https://geminicli.com/docs/",[6598],{"_73":1352,"_50":6587},"Can help understand game projects, edit scripts, and drive editors through MCP. The official README states that Antigravity CLI replaced Gemini CLI for unpaid-tier and Google One users on June 18, 2026, and that Gemini CLI is not optimized for the latest Gemini models. Check the account-specific migration guidance before choosing this entry point.",[6604],[4220,6592,4181,5144,6593],[1653,1470,1562],[247,126,293],{"_73":5015,"_50":6596},"resource:claude-code","A coding agent that reads and edits projects, runs tools, and supports skills, hooks, and MCP through terminal and IDE interfaces.",{"_44":944,"_1363":936,"_1361":5913,"_71":4817,"_1362":6606,"_1357":6634,"_50":6633,"_81":6635,"_1338":6636,"_1333":6637,"_1330":6638,"_1321":1395},[6609,6610,6611,6612,6613,6614,6615,6616,6617,6618,6619,6620,6621],{"_71":46,"_75":936,"_77":1363,"_79":-7},{"_71":124,"_75":6606,"_77":1362,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1360,"_75":5912,"_77":1361,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1358,"_75":4816,"_77":71,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_73":1355,"_75":6634,"_77":1357,"_79":80},{"_71":81,"_73":1352,"_83":6631,"_77":50,"_79":-7},{"_71":81,"_73":1344,"_83":6628,"_77":81,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1336,"_1327":1328,"_83":6626,"_77":1338,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1331,"_1327":1328,"_83":6625,"_77":1333,"_79":-7},{"_71":1325,"_73":1326,"_1327":1328,"_83":6624,"_77":1330,"_79":-7},{"_71":72,"_73":1319,"_75":1395,"_77":1321,"_79":111},{"_71":72,"_77":1316,"_73":1317,"_75":6296},{"_71":81,"_77":1311,"_73":1312,"_83":6622},[6623],{"_73":6180,"_50":6295},[232,109,286],[1637,1447,1545,2294],[4220,6627,4181,6075,6302],"General-purpose agent",[6629],{"_73":6630,"_50":6295},"Official repository and examples",[6632],{"_73":1352,"_50":6633},"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/overview","Can develop game scripts, migrate architecture, troubleshoot builds, and connect to Unity, Godot, or UE through community MCP servers. Use CLAUDE.md, skills, and editor state together; one MCP demonstration does not establish complete engine automation.",[6639],[4220,6627,4181,6075,6302],[1653,1470,1562,2332],[247,126,293],{"_73":6630,"_50":6295},"resource:codex","A general-purpose coding agent for reading, editing, running commands, and reviewing code in a local repository.",{"_44":1174,"_1363":1167,"_1361":5913,"_71":4817,"_136